# Default account — used when --account is omitted.
SKLIK_API_TOKEN=your-api-token-here

# Optional: additional named logins. Each --account <name> reads
# SKLIK_API_TOKEN_<NAME>. Add as many as you need (or delete this).
# Example below is selected with: --account clientb
# SKLIK_API_TOKEN_CLIENTB=your-other-api-token-here

# --- Fénix API (Seznam Nákupy: feed, diagnostics, shopping stats; fenix-*) ---
# A SEPARATE API with a SEPARATE token — the DRAK token above does not work
# here. Generate a Fénix refresh token in the Sklik web UI. Needed only for
# the feed-* / nakupy-* / shop-items / fenix-* commands. The token's access
# level matters: read-only (r) is enough for listings, the fenix-*-create and
# fenix-negative-add/-remove commands need read-write (rw).
# Per named account: SKLIK_FENIX_REFRESH_TOKEN_<NAME> / SKLIK_FENIX_PREMISE_<NAME>.
# SKLIK_FENIX_REFRESH_TOKEN=your-fenix-refresh-token-here
# SKLIK_FENIX_PREMISE=your-shop-premise-id      # default for --premise-id

# --- OPTIONAL: tokens in a password manager instead of this file ---
# Nothing above changes: plain tokens in .env + ./run.sh keep working.
# If you would rather not keep long-lived tokens on disk, put 1Password
# secret references here instead of the values and start the app through
# ./run-op.sh (it runs `op run --env-file=.env -- ./run.sh …`):
# SKLIK_API_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# SKLIK_FENIX_REFRESH_TOKEN=op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
# <field> is `credential` for an "API Credential" item and `notesPlain` for a
# "Secure Note". Details: README.md, section "Tokeny ve správci hesel".
